# Start during the movie leaves the opening for the title screen. Exercises
# the movie teardown path (lbMthp_8001F800) and a scene transition driven by
# real input rather than by a timer.
#
# Note this case deliberately crosses a scene load, which is where the two
# sides are least likely to stay in step: Dolphin pays real DVD latency and
# the port reads a local directory. The frame numbers after the press are
# therefore the interesting measurement, not an assumption.
description: press Start during the movie, land on the title
run_frames: 400
align: movie
input: 240: start
checks: 200, 260, 320
